WEBVTT

00:15.780 --> 00:19.910
I never thought death could be so depressing.

00:22.620 --> 00:26.250
Does having a powerful spirit
really mean anything?

00:26.790 --> 00:29.790
Where did you get that key spirit?

00:29.790 --> 00:33.750
You don't even know what you have?!

00:34.700 --> 00:36.990
What is a key spirit?

00:39.730 --> 00:41.530
Zed, Roya...

00:42.670 --> 00:44.970
Guzma, Lucia...

00:45.570 --> 00:48.880
We are truly indebted to the two of you.

00:48.880 --> 00:52.710
We're able to live on thanks to you both.

00:52.710 --> 00:54.980
It's not like that.

00:54.980 --> 00:57.650
Is everyone really going to leave here?

00:57.650 --> 00:59.720
Yes, if we stay here,

00:59.720 --> 01:04.060
it's only a matter of time before Zymot
sends someone to attack us again.

01:04.060 --> 01:06.390
It's difficult to abandon your own homeland.

01:06.390 --> 01:09.160
But if all of us survivors work together,

01:09.160 --> 01:11.290
we're sure to find somewhere to live peacefully.

01:12.100 --> 01:15.730
We're also doing it so that Princess Rebecca's
and Kemp's deaths will not have been in vain.

01:16.740 --> 01:20.680
We've named this little girl Rebecca.

01:20.680 --> 01:23.380
We'll raise her with love,

01:23.380 --> 01:26.010
and think of her as though she were
Princess Rebecca herself reborn.

01:27.080 --> 01:28.710
Rebecca...

01:41.900 --> 01:49.640
We've all surely got our arms outstretched

01:49.640 --> 01:56.600
Towards a far, faraway place

02:09.960 --> 02:16.160
Blown by the wind, we walk on

02:16.160 --> 02:23.130
Wanting to know the reason we were born

02:23.340 --> 02:29.640
Even if a time of loss should come

02:29.640 --> 02:36.780
Let's now choose to hold each other tight

02:39.220 --> 02:46.630
We've all surely got our arms outstretched

02:46.630 --> 02:52.600
Towards something we can't lose

02:52.600 --> 03:00.240
Pulling only brilliant dreams closer

03:00.240 --> 03:07.110
Towards a far, faraway place

03:21.660 --> 03:23.400
Here he is!

03:23.400 --> 03:24.030
Damn!

03:24.030 --> 03:25.830
Get him!
Damn!

03:25.830 --> 03:27.460
Stop!

03:29.240 --> 03:31.740
I'm not getting caught in a place like this!

03:31.740 --> 03:33.710
I'm going to be free!

03:36.280 --> 03:40.300
Episode 19
A Dark Land

03:50.890 --> 03:52.330
Now we've got him cornered!

03:52.330 --> 03:54.120
Don't dare lose him!

03:58.230 --> 03:59.860
Stop!

04:02.470 --> 04:05.910
Did he have a shifting shard stashed away here?

04:05.910 --> 04:08.310
At any rate, we must report this
before anything else!

04:08.310 --> 04:09.610
Right!

04:19.750 --> 04:22.920
Oh, I'm pooped!

04:22.920 --> 04:27.230
We'll never finish such a huge
hallway in a single day.

04:27.230 --> 04:31.690
Well, yeah, I admit we went to Kalb-Hu
without permission, but still...

04:32.530 --> 04:36.160
Hey, Zed, let's get Mickey to help us out!

04:38.110 --> 04:41.210
Hey! Say something, Zed!

04:41.210 --> 04:43.540
Shut up, put a lid on it!

04:43.540 --> 04:46.010
Well, you do a better job of this yourself!

04:47.750 --> 04:50.880
He's been like that the whole time
since we got back from Kalb-Hu.

04:54.890 --> 04:57.360
Now that I think about it, that woman...

04:58.890 --> 05:01.360
Ro..Roya...

05:02.230 --> 05:04.360
How did she know my name?

05:05.800 --> 05:09.540
Well, well, are you doing the job right now?

05:09.540 --> 05:11.170
Master Zico!

05:11.170 --> 05:13.410
This is boring me out of my mind.

05:13.410 --> 05:15.410
You help out too, old man.

05:15.410 --> 05:18.810
You two ought to appreciate that
you've gotten off

05:18.810 --> 05:20.820
with as light a punishment as this.

05:20.820 --> 05:22.280
Zico!

05:22.280 --> 05:25.150
That escaped convict has been captured!

05:25.150 --> 05:27.760
Oh, is that so now?

05:27.760 --> 05:29.550
Escaped convict?

05:33.760 --> 05:35.000
Do tell!

05:35.000 --> 05:39.130
So, a Neotopian convict has escaped
into Templar, you say?

05:40.230 --> 05:42.870
We have already apprehended the escapee.

05:42.870 --> 05:47.000
I would like to have you take this escaped
convict back to Neotopia.

05:48.180 --> 05:50.580
You can forget it.

05:50.580 --> 05:52.150
Listen, guys...

05:52.150 --> 05:54.650
I've had to put up with quite a
few troublesome jobs

05:54.650 --> 05:56.620
since I became shard champion of
Templar, wouldn't you say?

05:59.320 --> 06:00.320
I've got it.

06:00.320 --> 06:02.620
Why not let Zed handle the matter?

06:02.620 --> 06:03.990
Zed?

06:03.990 --> 06:06.460
It doesn't sound like such a difficult task.

06:06.460 --> 06:08.430
He can handle it.

06:21.280 --> 06:22.740
Come on, Sagiri.

06:22.740 --> 06:24.350
Time to get up.

06:24.350 --> 06:27.580
Let me sleep a little longer...

06:27.580 --> 06:30.020
Sagiri, that will not do.

06:30.020 --> 06:32.520
You get up after the morning bell has rung.

06:32.520 --> 06:34.320
That's the rule, right?

06:35.490 --> 06:38.760
Sagiri, that is this country's rule.

06:38.760 --> 06:41.060
If you don't get up, it's a crime.

06:41.060 --> 06:43.160
All right...

06:43.160 --> 06:45.460
You want me to go report this
to the people upstairs?

06:47.300 --> 06:49.300
All right...

06:49.300 --> 06:51.430
There you go, good girl.

06:51.740 --> 06:55.040
They wouldn't know if you
didn't tell them though.

06:55.410 --> 06:59.040
Slacking off like that will lead
to failure in other things.

07:00.980 --> 07:02.950
You understand, don't you?

07:03.320 --> 07:05.110
Thanks for the food!

07:05.790 --> 07:09.960
Sagiri, that won't do, you left some.

07:09.960 --> 07:13.460
The calories in these meals are
precisely calculated

07:13.460 --> 07:16.830
with each individual's health in mind.

07:16.830 --> 07:19.430
That's why the rules say you
mustn't leave any of...

07:19.430 --> 07:21.230
I'm sorry!

07:23.140 --> 07:26.070
Noah, have you finished your meal yet?

07:26.070 --> 07:27.910
Yes, just now.

07:27.910 --> 07:29.310
I see...

07:29.310 --> 07:31.950
I would like to speak with you a moment.

07:31.950 --> 07:34.070
Certainly, let's step outside then.

07:35.250 --> 07:37.050
See you later!

07:40.090 --> 07:42.060
It's a nice day, isn't it?

07:42.820 --> 07:46.780
Neotopia is peaceful and beautiful again today.

07:50.330 --> 07:52.100
Peace in Neotopia is owed to law and order,

07:52.100 --> 07:55.800
which permeate every aspect of life here.

07:55.800 --> 07:58.100
Law is everything.

07:59.410 --> 08:02.440
The tragedies you once experienced

08:02.440 --> 08:05.740
were all brought about by the
disruption of this order.

08:06.780 --> 08:08.650
I trust you agree?

08:08.650 --> 08:10.280
Yes...

08:11.690 --> 08:14.960
You are the chosen one.

08:14.960 --> 08:19.760
I want you to use your power to protect the
people's happiness and peace in this country.

08:21.460 --> 08:24.400
That is my wish,

08:24.400 --> 08:27.640
as it is the wish of everyone else.

08:27.640 --> 08:29.430
Everyone's wish?

08:32.110 --> 08:34.980
I will if I'm able to.

08:34.980 --> 08:37.100
That is wonderful, Noah.

08:44.350 --> 08:47.660
I believe you have already
heard the story from Zico.

08:47.660 --> 08:53.230
Zed, we will leave you with the task
of escorting this escaped convict.

08:53.230 --> 08:56.360
But are you really sure we can rely on Zed?

08:58.170 --> 09:02.940
Regardless of whatever alliance we
of Neotopia may have with you,

09:02.940 --> 09:05.910
if there were to be any problems
at a critical time like this,

09:05.910 --> 09:08.210
I assure you it would be a disaster.

09:09.510 --> 09:13.580
I'm saying I'll go, so there's no problem.

09:13.580 --> 09:16.420
That attitude is a problem too.

09:16.420 --> 09:18.210
Agreed!

09:18.950 --> 09:21.920
I shall take full responsibility.

09:22.920 --> 09:25.720
Is that satisfactory, my colleagues?

09:30.570 --> 09:36.700
From here on, each of your experiences
will be critical to your development.

09:37.510 --> 09:39.910
Be mindful of this.

09:39.910 --> 09:41.530
Right.

09:44.310 --> 09:50.180
I am surprised you accepted this
mission as openly as you did.

09:50.180 --> 09:53.290
There's no point in only becoming stronger.

09:53.290 --> 09:56.260
I have a feeling there's something
else you need too.

10:01.200 --> 10:02.860
Hey, old man...

10:02.860 --> 10:06.130
Why did Amir Gaul choose me?

10:06.130 --> 10:08.260
What the heck is a key spirit?!

10:11.270 --> 10:14.780
Explaining it in words is simple enough.

10:14.780 --> 10:18.850
However, I doubt you will take
those words to heart.

10:18.850 --> 10:20.780
Don't go judging me however you like!

10:20.780 --> 10:23.080
Build your experience!

10:24.090 --> 10:26.120
Learn it through your body.

10:26.120 --> 10:29.090
You must feel it in your heart.

10:29.090 --> 10:30.890
Got it?

10:35.600 --> 10:41.540
I see, so he has at last stumbled upon
the reality of key spirits, has he?

10:41.540 --> 10:44.330
Do you think he'll be all right at this rate, Zico?

10:45.440 --> 10:47.270
Just a little longer.

10:47.270 --> 10:52.210
But what will we do if the worst
happens to Zed?

10:52.210 --> 10:53.880
If and when it comes to that,

10:53.880 --> 10:58.020
then this feeble, old fool will lay down his life.

10:58.020 --> 11:01.320
I mustn't let myself repeat the same mistake.

11:03.960 --> 11:05.590
Mater Zico!

11:06.930 --> 11:08.760
What is it, Roya?

11:08.760 --> 11:11.390
There's something I simply have to ask you.

11:13.400 --> 11:17.360
About my parents, who supposedly
died when I was young...

11:18.410 --> 11:21.710
What would you want to know at this point?

11:21.710 --> 11:26.010
Did my parents really die in the war?

11:26.010 --> 11:27.980
Yes...

11:27.980 --> 11:31.690
Then, please explain exactly how it happened!

11:31.690 --> 11:33.650
How did they die?

11:33.650 --> 11:35.160
How did they dress?

11:35.160 --> 11:37.120
What was my father like?

11:37.120 --> 11:38.260
How about my mother?

11:38.260 --> 11:40.560
Did my mother look like me?!

11:44.030 --> 11:46.000
I'm sorry!

11:55.710 --> 11:57.680
Okay, begin.

12:02.950 --> 12:04.580
Damn!

12:05.950 --> 12:07.590
Let go!

12:07.590 --> 12:08.820
No! Roya will be...

12:08.820 --> 12:09.820
No!
No! Roya will be...

12:09.820 --> 12:12.360
I don't want to go back to Neotopia!

12:12.360 --> 12:14.160
No!

12:16.530 --> 12:18.630
There's nothing we can do now.

12:18.630 --> 12:21.600
Let's contact Neotopia and let them know.

12:23.400 --> 12:25.030
Roya...

12:30.310 --> 12:33.850
What? Shifting energy emanating from Templar?

12:33.850 --> 12:34.920
Yes, sire.

12:34.920 --> 12:36.750
It seems to have been three people,

12:36.750 --> 12:40.710
one of whose signature indicated a
particularly powerful spirit shard.

12:42.360 --> 12:43.820
Can you bring them down?

12:43.820 --> 12:48.630
Yes, sire, however, we believe
they may fall into Tusk...

12:48.630 --> 12:51.000
Tusk, eh?

12:51.000 --> 12:52.800
No choice, bring them down.

12:52.800 --> 12:54.300
Sire!

12:54.300 --> 12:56.340
I will head into Tusk as well.

12:56.340 --> 12:57.960
Sire!

13:12.420 --> 13:14.820
I feel sick...

13:14.820 --> 13:18.760
What the heck were those vibrations
during our shifting?

13:18.760 --> 13:20.360
Don’t know...

13:20.360 --> 13:23.300
This isn't Neotopia.

13:23.300 --> 13:25.300
What?!

13:25.300 --> 13:28.170
Then, where the heck are we?

13:28.170 --> 13:30.300
It's incredibly cold.

13:31.210 --> 13:34.910
No doubt about it, this is Tusk.

13:34.910 --> 13:36.280
Tusk?

13:36.280 --> 13:37.750
What's Tusk?

13:37.750 --> 13:41.480
A nation allied with Zymot, an enemy.

13:41.480 --> 13:42.480
Enemy?

13:42.480 --> 13:46.720
Master Zico told me it is a land we are
forbidden from approaching

13:46.720 --> 13:49.460
under any circumstances.

13:49.460 --> 13:51.790
Tusk is the holy land of Tusker.

13:51.790 --> 13:53.030
Tusker?

13:53.030 --> 13:55.860
Tusker is said to have created all these lands,

13:55.860 --> 13:58.800
and is virtually a god to the people of Tusk.

13:58.800 --> 14:01.470
I heard they've been gathering
countless spirit shards

14:01.470 --> 14:05.270
from far and wide, with the aim
of resurrecting Tusker.

14:07.340 --> 14:10.180
Countless spirit shards...

14:10.180 --> 14:13.310
We've landed in a bad place.

14:13.310 --> 14:16.680
They'll come after shard casters for sure.

14:16.680 --> 14:18.480
Watch your backs.

14:19.350 --> 14:22.650
But why did we end up in Tusk?

14:26.590 --> 14:30.160
Hand over your spirit now!

14:30.160 --> 14:31.400
Quiet!

14:31.400 --> 14:33.200
Get him, Kaon!

14:38.570 --> 14:42.010
That big one's got to be a beast man.

14:42.010 --> 14:43.710
Beast man?

14:43.710 --> 14:45.050
I've heard there are two races of Tuskans:

14:45.050 --> 14:48.480
beast men, like that big guy, who are
huge and have four arms;

14:48.480 --> 14:54.050
and humans that have horns growing
out of their shoulders.

14:54.050 --> 14:55.620
Horns in their shoulders?!

14:55.620 --> 14:59.080
I must kill that kid!

15:01.760 --> 15:04.730
As I thought, sent from Tusk, are you?

15:06.130 --> 15:08.430
So, she was talking about them!

15:09.270 --> 15:11.070
Kill that guy!

15:36.460 --> 15:40.530
Do beast men fight spirits head-on?

15:40.530 --> 15:43.300
It looks like they can...

15:43.300 --> 15:46.930
...somehow form shards inside their own bodies.

15:48.340 --> 15:51.080
What? They fell into Tusk, you say?!

15:51.080 --> 15:52.510
Yes...

15:52.510 --> 15:55.120
It appears that much is certain.

15:55.120 --> 15:59.420
They are currently investigating how
this could have happened.

15:59.420 --> 16:04.220
Even so, that it should be Tusk
of all places, well...

16:06.460 --> 16:08.260
Roya...

16:09.000 --> 16:11.170
Boy, I am counting on you.

16:11.170 --> 16:14.130
Protect Roya!

16:31.990 --> 16:33.550
I smell it...

16:33.550 --> 16:35.160
I smell them!

16:35.160 --> 16:37.990
I smell shard casters!

16:37.990 --> 16:39.490
What do we do?

16:39.490 --> 16:42.330
He's going to find us if we stay here!

16:42.330 --> 16:44.160
We'll have to fight him.

16:44.160 --> 16:47.000
Then, hey, take these off. Okay?

16:47.000 --> 16:49.340
Forget it, stay here and don't get any ideas.

16:49.340 --> 16:51.130
Oh, okay.

16:53.070 --> 16:54.700
What the...

16:59.110 --> 17:02.080
I don't come across many shard casters like you.

17:07.990 --> 17:09.620
Zed!

17:09.990 --> 17:14.190
Ooh! Now, here's a pretty, little thing!

17:14.190 --> 17:16.760
If I offer her to King Gari as a sacrificial victim,

17:16.760 --> 17:20.220
he will no doubt be delighted!

17:25.710 --> 17:26.710
Damn!

17:26.710 --> 17:28.500
I'm your opponent!

17:41.290 --> 17:44.220
You'd like me to go to Tusk?

17:44.220 --> 17:45.530
Yes...

17:45.530 --> 17:48.860
An escaped convict, who was supposed
to have been escorted back here,

17:48.860 --> 17:51.500
has fallen into Tusk by mistake.

17:51.500 --> 17:53.370
Escaped convict?

17:53.370 --> 17:57.500
It is a man named Keith, whom
you know from Ratt Village.

17:58.240 --> 18:00.010
Keith...

18:00.010 --> 18:03.710
He escaped after being imprisoned
for high treason.

18:03.710 --> 18:08.340
Naturally, high treason is a crime punishable
by the death penalty.

18:09.820 --> 18:12.120
You'll accept this mission, will you not?

18:14.490 --> 18:16.120
Yes!

18:23.230 --> 18:25.600
Standing around like this won't help us.

18:25.600 --> 18:29.700
We need to think of some way
to shift out of here.

18:29.700 --> 18:31.670
You're right.

18:31.670 --> 18:34.910
For starters, I guess we should scope out
our surroundings, huh?

18:34.910 --> 18:36.640
Before that...

18:36.640 --> 18:38.610
Do you think you could take this off?

18:38.610 --> 18:39.610
Forget it.

18:39.610 --> 18:41.240
Oh, okay.

18:48.560 --> 18:51.890
Thanks for saving me back there.

18:51.890 --> 18:53.730
Don't worry about it.

18:53.730 --> 18:58.530
Say, you really don't look like a criminal.

18:58.530 --> 19:00.330
What did you do?

19:01.570 --> 19:03.370
Treason.

19:04.170 --> 19:05.970
Treason?!

19:06.440 --> 19:09.840
It was because I hate the country of Neotopia.

19:09.840 --> 19:12.780
But it's the place you were born, isn't it?

19:12.780 --> 19:16.280
Oh, I do love the place I was born.

19:16.280 --> 19:20.240
But I can't stomach the "ideals"
the government sells.

19:24.190 --> 19:27.490
The military rescued me when I
was on the verge of death,

19:27.490 --> 19:31.470
but it was only so that they could use
my execution as an example.

19:31.470 --> 19:35.270
In that country, they'll kill a person as
readily as they squash an insect.

19:36.240 --> 19:37.600
How could that be?

19:37.600 --> 19:40.900
I've heard Neotopia is a magnificent country.

19:41.780 --> 19:43.640
It only appears that way.

19:43.640 --> 19:46.110
If you lived there, you'd know right away.

20:03.860 --> 20:05.970
Welcome to Tusk.

20:05.970 --> 20:08.170
But to see you coming here on your own

20:08.170 --> 20:10.670
makes me think it is a matter of great import.

20:10.670 --> 20:15.440
No, I am merely stopping by, have no fear.

20:15.440 --> 20:17.570
The king awaits.

20:24.750 --> 20:27.720
Well met, Hugh.

20:29.220 --> 20:33.520
King Gari, it is an honor to
meet you, your majesty.

20:35.500 --> 20:37.730
Can you see anything?

20:37.730 --> 20:39.800
I don't see a thing.

20:39.800 --> 20:42.540
The Tuskans live here.

20:42.540 --> 20:45.510
There's got to be a castle or something around.

20:49.880 --> 20:51.380
We're surrounded.

20:51.380 --> 20:53.180
Looks like it.

21:01.460 --> 21:04.290
Please! Let me fight too!

21:04.290 --> 21:05.290
Forget it!

21:05.290 --> 21:07.590
We're delivering you safely to Neotopia.

21:16.600 --> 21:18.230
Rambos!

21:28.950 --> 21:30.750
He's tough...

21:41.190 --> 21:42.820
Apcarel!

21:43.460 --> 21:45.000
Roya, are you all right?

21:45.000 --> 21:46.230
Yeah...

21:46.230 --> 21:48.030
Behind you!

21:51.340 --> 21:52.570
Zed!

21:52.570 --> 21:52.810
Zed!

21:52.810 --> 21:54.430
Roya!
Zed!

21:54.570 --> 21:56.200
Damn...

21:58.850 --> 22:00.470
Zed!

22:29.680 --> 22:31.800
So, this is Tusk?

22:41.920 --> 22:44.520
Open the hands you have over your face

22:44.520 --> 22:47.360
It looks like you'll be done in by the sun

22:47.360 --> 22:52.320
Let's let the sky melt away our melancholy

22:52.670 --> 22:58.310
We stripped off our heavy jackets
and started running, 6, 7, 8

22:58.310 --> 23:04.270
So, we'll make the wind blow in this
windless place, and take off! Go!

23:09.320 --> 23:14.720
I'm shaken awake, head spinning,
and sunlight hits me the next moment

23:14.720 --> 23:18.520
The rain's abatement lets loose dreams

23:20.230 --> 23:22.960
We'll dash down this path

23:22.960 --> 23:30.430
Search for the one-and-only "now"
and our heartbeats

23:31.100 --> 23:33.770
Thrust out our clasped hands

23:33.770 --> 23:36.540
It looks like we could even shatter the sun

23:36.540 --> 23:41.500
Let's launch our melancholy into the sky

23:42.020 --> 23:47.550
Try again, step forward, if we're hesitating 7, 8, 9

23:47.550 --> 23:53.690
We'll shout loud enough to echo
to Cloud Ten, and go!

24:16.950 --> 24:20.950
Next Time
Reunion

24:18.250 --> 24:20.950


Next time, "Reunion"
